								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=371"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16874#msg16874"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16874#msg16874">Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2904 on:</b> May 04, 2005, 02:03:32 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Is it fair to people with the last name Hitler that they&#039;re judged based on that name?&nbsp; Probably not.&nbsp; Is it fair that people are judged based on the color of their skin?&nbsp; Definitely not.&nbsp; Is it fair to judge a guild, including its newer members, by the history of that guild?&nbsp; Maybe.&nbsp; You choose to wear a guild tag and you get the good and the bad of that guild.&nbsp; That&#039;s why it&#039;s so important to play honorably, and for guilds to police their own and make sure their members don&#039;t cheat, KS, train, etc.&nbsp; Because in EQ, when you&#039;re guilded, what you do is held in favor of or against your guid.&nbsp; And people have very long memories.&nbsp; Just because some of the officers are changed or the membership is altered (people always coming and going in any guild) doesn&#039;t mean that guild history, good or bad, is wiped clean.&nbsp; I honestly think that that&#039;s part of the uniqueness of the game, the social interaction and the history.&nbsp; The lack of competition in today&#039;s EQ, due to instancing of content, means that guilds have far fewer chances to interact (race, KS, cockblock, set up rotations, etc.), either for good or bad, than they used to.&nbsp; So there&#039;s really less opportunity for reputations to develop or change than there used to be.<br /><br />I&#039;m still sad TA and JH are gone.&nbsp; Two very cool guilds, and cool people.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><img src="http://i3.photobucket.com/albums/y68/tvsbill/6fbdd1b6.jpg" alt="" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
