							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg16874#msg16874">Quote from: Shakro on May 04, 2005, 02:03:32 pm</a></div><div class="quote">Is it fair to people with the last name Hitler that they&#039;re judged based on that name?  Probably not.  Is it fair that people are judged based on the color of their skin?  Definitely not.  Is it fair to judge a guild, including its newer members, by the history of that guild?  Maybe.  You choose to wear a guild tag and you get the good and the bad of that guild.  That&#039;s why it&#039;s so important to play honorably, and for guilds to police their own and make sure their members don&#039;t cheat, KS, train, etc.  Because in EQ, when you&#039;re guilded, what you do is held in favor of or against your guid.  And people have very long memories.  Just because some of the officers are changed or the membership is altered (people always coming and going in any guild) doesn&#039;t mean that guild history, good or bad, is wiped clean.  I honestly think that that&#039;s part of the uniqueness of the game, the social interaction and the history.  The lack of competition in today&#039;s EQ, due to instancing of content, means that guilds have far fewer chances to interact (race, KS, cockblock, set up rotations, etc.), either for good or bad, than they used to.  So there&#039;s really less opportunity for reputations to develop or change than there used to be.<br /><br />I&#039;m still sad TA and JH are gone.  Two very cool guilds, and cool people.<br /></div><br />i agree that history of the guild cantr just disappear but a good deal of members have changed as well as officers. its a whole diffrent guild now and you cant blame current mebers for screw ups in the past yah it was wrong and yah they strill did it, but dont use it against us now as a point when the guild has been through a huge change.
						</td>
					</tr>
